Z||000017||BAM-BAM||04-14-2001||01:10 AM||||  This is the end of the 3800SC story, at least in as much as my 85GT is concerned. I talked to Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero and he basicaly scared the hell out of me about this swap. In fact he had me so intemidated that I ran down to my pontiac dealer and ordered a brand new 93-95 Camaro 3.4l crate engine. Now I won't have to wory about tranmissions, ECM's, harnesses, what fits, what don't, who has the best parts, who is the shiester, none of that. This past three days I have been in a tornado of this's and that's, whos's and what's, why's and why not's. I have been jerk around twice on some smok'n deals on 3800SC engines W/trans ect. I have been told that the swap of my dreams was going to be a cluster F---! and that it would never work right. So I said to myself, myself I said, FORGET IT!!! I'll just do the standard +1. I wanted a new engine with increased HP and torque and that is what I am getting. and all for $2225.00 out the door. I can make some moderate adjustments and improvements and I know I'll be pleased, maybe not as extremely as I expected, but pleased none the less.<BR>  Now, I want to thank everyone who has endured this rukus with me. This Forum is the only sane place I have been in the past two day's, even my family is going insane (I have that effect on them). Special thanks to TerryK for all the GOOD info and advice he has provided. I will take you up on that offer in a short time. Owenslee, Kerry, I appologize for keeping you on hold, not intentional. And to the rest of yous guys and gals, thanks for lending me your eyes for time it took to read my babble. This truly is a great place and I'm glad to be back from hiatus.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
